# .dockerignore  [What never enters the image]
# Stage 3   The local Python project becomes a container; describe which files may enter it
#           Excluding data, notebooks and secrets keeps the serving image small and safe
# Purpose   Keep the image small and safe: no data, notebooks, tests or secrets
# Strategy  Allow-list: ignore everything, then allow only what the API needs
#           (Dockerfile, conda-lock.yml, config.yaml, src/, models/ (the promoted model, baked in at release))
# Safety    .env and caches are excluded even if a rule above changes
